IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `fwa2-common`

-- Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth) -- baseline-2026-11: what a court can order when a civil remedy provision is broken.
--
-- SEAT: the employee, worker or contractor who brings (or is thinking of bringing) the court case: "What is the most my
-- employer can be ordered to pay as a penalty? Was it a serious contravention? Can I sue the manager or director too,
-- or the franchisor or parent company? Will I get interest? Can I be made to pay the other side's costs?"
--
-- PROVISIONS. s 539(2) table items 1, 2, 10, 11, 11A, 11B, 27A, 27B and 38 (column 4, maximum penalties) and the
-- s 12 definition of "selected civil remedy provision"; s 546(2), (2A), (2AA) (the penalty for individuals, bodies
-- corporate and multiples of the underpayment); s 546A(1) (associated with an underpayment); s 557A(1), (2), (5A) and
-- s 557B(1) (serious contravention); s 550 (people involved); s 558B(1)-(3) with s 558A (franchisors and holding
-- companies); s 547 (interest); s 570 (costs). The penalty unit's dollar value comes from fwa2-common.l4. Out: the
-- other s 539 items; s 545 (encoded so far as underpayments go in baseline-2026-10); ss 548 (small claims; ditto),
-- 549, 551-556, 558 (infringement notices), 558C, 569, 569A, 571.
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 73 (register id C2026C00355), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2009A00028.txt.
-- BASELINE; see NOTES.md.

§ `Fair Work Act 2009 -- what a court can order, from the seat of the person bringing the case`

§§ `ss 539, 546, 557A -- the most the other side can be ordered to pay as a penalty`

-- s 539(2), column 4, for the provisions this encoding meets:
--   item 1 (s 44, the NES), item 2 (s 45, modern awards), item 10 (ss 323(1), 323(3), 325(1), 328): "for a serious
--     contravention--600 penalty units; or otherwise--60 penalty units";
--   item 11 (ss 340, 343-346, 348-355, 369(3): the general protections): 60 penalty units;
--   item 11A (ss 357(1), 358, 359: sham contracting): 60 penalty units;
--   item 11B (ss 359B, 359C: sham casual employment): 300 penalty units;
--   item 27A (s 527D(1): sexual harassment) and item 27B (s 527K: a stop sexual harassment order): 60 penalty units;
--   item 38 (s 789FG: an order to stop bullying): 60 penalty units.
-- s 12: "selected civil remedy provision means a provision referred to in column 1 of item 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 7, 8, 9, 10,
-- 10A, 10F, 11A, 29, 29AA, 29A, 32, 33, 33A, 34 or 34AAA" -- of those here, items 1, 2, 10 and 11A.
DECLARE `Provision broken` IS ONE OF
    `the NES (s 44)`
    `a modern award (s 45)`
    `paying in full, in money, or an unreasonable requirement to pay (ss 323, 325)`
    `the general protections (ss 340, 351, 352 and others in item 11)`
    `sham contracting (ss 357-359)`
    `sham casual employment (ss 359B, 359C)`
    `sexual harassment (s 527D)`
    `a stop sexual harassment order (s 527K)`
    `an order to stop bullying (s 789FG)`

GIVEN `the provision` IS A `Provision broken`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the item has a serious contravention tier` IS
    CONSIDER `the provision`
    WHEN `the NES (s 44)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a modern award (s 45)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `paying in full, in money, or an unreasonable requirement to pay (ss 323, 325)` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the provision` IS A `Provision broken`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a selected civil remedy provision` IS
    CONSIDER `the provision`
    WHEN `the NES (s 44)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a modern award (s 45)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `paying in full, in money, or an unreasonable requirement to pay (ss 323, 325)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `sham contracting (ss 357-359)` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the provision` IS A `Provision broken`, `it was a serious contravention` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the column 4 penalty units` MEANS
    IF `the item has a serious contravention tier` `the provision` AND `it was a serious contravention`
    THEN 600
    ELSE CONSIDER `the provision`
         WHEN `sham casual employment (ss 359B, 359C)` THEN 300
         OTHERWISE 60

-- s 557A(1): "A contravention ... is a serious contravention if: (a) the person knowingly contravened the provision; or
-- (b) the person was reckless as to whether the contravention would occur." (2): reckless if "(a) the person is aware of
-- a substantial risk that the contravention would occur; and (b) having regard to the circumstances known to the person,
-- it is unjustifiable to take the risk." s 557B(1): "a body corporate knowingly contravenes ... if the body corporate
-- expressly, tacitly or impliedly authorised the contravention." (5A): a person involved commits a serious contravention
-- "only if: (a) the principal's contravention was a serious contravention; and (b) the involved person knew" it was.
DECLARE `Who broke it` IS ONE OF
    `an individual who broke it themselves`
    `a company or other body corporate that broke it`
    `a person involved in my employer's contravention (s 550)`

@export Was it a serious contravention, carrying the higher maximum penalty (ss 557A, 557B)?
GIVEN `who broke it` IS A `Who broke it` @desc Who you are asking about: an individual who broke it themselves (an employer who is a sole trader, a harasser); a company or other body corporate that broke it; or a person involved in your employer's contravention (a manager, director or adviser)
      `they knew they were breaking it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they knowingly broke the provision (for a company: whether it expressly, tacitly or impliedly authorised the contravention); they need not know the exact amount
      `they were aware of a substantial risk of breaking it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they were aware of a substantial risk that the contravention would happen
      `taking that risk was unjustifiable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on the circumstances they knew, it was unjustifiable to take that risk
      `my employer's contravention was serious` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a person involved: whether your employer's own contravention was a serious contravention
      `they knew my employer's contravention was serious` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a person involved: whether they knew your employer's contravention was a serious contravention
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was it a serious contravention` IS
    CONSIDER `who broke it`
    WHEN `a person involved in my employer's contravention (s 550)` THEN
            `my employer's contravention was serious`
        AND `they knew my employer's contravention was serious`
    OTHERWISE
            `they knew they were breaking it`
        OR  (`they were aware of a substantial risk of breaking it` AND `taking that risk was unjustifiable`)

-- s 546(2): the penalty "must not be more than: (a) if the person is an individual--the maximum number of penalty units
-- referred to in the relevant item in column 4 ...; or (b) if the person is a body corporate--5 times" that number.
-- s 546(2AA): "if: (a) the civil remedy provision is a selected civil remedy provision; and (b) the person is a body
-- corporate; and (c) when the application for the order is made, the person is not a small business employer; the
-- pecuniary penalty must not be more than 5 times the amount worked out in accordance with paragraph (2)(b)."
-- (s 23: a small business employer has "fewer than 15 employees", counting regular casuals and associated entities.)
GIVEN `the provision` IS A `Provision broken`
      `who broke it` IS A `Who broke it`
      `it was a serious contravention` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company had fewer than 15 employees when the case was filed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 546 penalty units` MEANS
    CONSIDER `who broke it`
    WHEN `a company or other body corporate that broke it` THEN
        IF     `it is a selected civil remedy provision` `the provision`
           AND (NOT `the company had fewer than 15 employees when the case was filed`)
        THEN 25 TIMES `the column 4 penalty units` `the provision` `it was a serious contravention`
        ELSE 5 TIMES `the column 4 penalty units` `the provision` `it was a serious contravention`
    OTHERWISE `the column 4 penalty units` `the provision` `it was a serious contravention`

@export What is the largest civil penalty, in penalty units, the court can order against the one who broke the provision (ss 539, 546(2), (2AA))?
GIVEN `the provision` IS A `Provision broken` @desc Which provision was broken: the NES (s 44); a modern award (s 45); paying in full or in money, or an unreasonable requirement to pay (ss 323, 325); the general protections (ss 340, 351, 352 and others); sham contracting (ss 357-359); sham casual employment (ss 359B, 359C); sexual harassment (s 527D); a stop sexual harassment order (s 527K); an order to stop bullying (s 789FG)
      `who broke it` IS A `Who broke it` @desc Who the penalty is sought against: an individual who broke it themselves; a company or other body corporate that broke it; or a person involved in the contravention (s 550)
      `it was a serious contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was a serious contravention -- knowing or reckless (ask the s 557A question); it matters only for the NES, awards and ss 323, 325
      `the company had fewer than 15 employees when the case was filed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, when the court application was made, the company employed fewer than 15 employees (counting regular casuals and associated entities): a small business employer
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the largest civil penalty in penalty units` MEANS
    `the s 546 penalty units` `the provision` `who broke it` `it was a serious contravention` `the company had fewer than 15 employees when the case was filed`

-- s 546(2A): "Despite paragraph (2)(b) and subsection (2AA), if: (a) the civil remedy provision is a selected civil
-- remedy provision; and (b) the person is a body corporate; and (c) when the application for the order is made, the
-- person is not a small business employer; and (d) the contravention is associated with an underpayment amount; and
-- (e) the application specifies that the applicant wants the maximum penalty to be calculated based on a multiple of the
-- underpayment amount; and (f) the person is not taken to have contravened the civil remedy provision under section 550
-- ...; the pecuniary penalty must not be more than the greater of the following: (g) the amount worked out in accordance
-- with subsection (2AA); (h) 3 times the underpayment amount."
-- s 546A(1): associated with an underpayment amount where a required amount was not paid in full by its due day and
-- "the failure is related to the contravention"; (2) the amount is the difference "to the extent it can be determined
-- by the court" (an input: 0 if none).
@export What is the largest civil penalty in dollars the court can order (ss 539, 546, 546A, with the penalty unit)?
GIVEN `the provision` IS A `Provision broken` @desc Which provision was broken: the NES (s 44); a modern award (s 45); paying in full or in money, or an unreasonable requirement to pay (ss 323, 325); the general protections; sham contracting (ss 357-359); sham casual employment; sexual harassment (s 527D); a stop sexual harassment order; an order to stop bullying
      `who broke it` IS A `Who broke it` @desc Who the penalty is sought against: an individual who broke it themselves; a company or other body corporate that broke it; or a person involved in the contravention (s 550)
      `it was a serious contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was a serious contravention -- knowing or reckless; it matters only for the NES, awards and ss 323, 325
      `the company had fewer than 15 employees when the case was filed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, when the court application was made, the company employed fewer than 15 employees (a small business employer)
      `the underpayment the court can determine` IS A NUMBER @desc The underpayment related to the contravention, as far as the court can determine it, in dollars (0 if none)
      `my application asks for a multiple of the underpayment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court application says the applicant wants the maximum penalty worked out as a multiple of the underpayment
      `the contravention happened on` IS A DATE @desc The day of the contravention, which fixes the dollar value of a penalty unit
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is the largest civil penalty in dollars` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the dollar value of a penalty unit for conduct on` `the contravention happened on`
    WHEN JUST `unit` THEN
        JUST (IF `the s 546(2A) multiple applies`
              THEN `the larger of` `the penalty in dollars` (3 TIMES `the underpayment the court can determine`)
              ELSE `the penalty in dollars`)
        WHERE
            `the penalty in dollars` MEANS
                `unit` TIMES (`What is the largest civil penalty in penalty units` `the provision` `who broke it` `it was a serious contravention` `the company had fewer than 15 employees when the case was filed`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHERE
        `the s 546(2A) multiple applies` MEANS
                `it is a selected civil remedy provision` `the provision`
            AND `the one who broke it is a company`
            AND (NOT `the company had fewer than 15 employees when the case was filed`)
            AND `the underpayment the court can determine` GREATER THAN 0
            AND `my application asks for a multiple of the underpayment`
        `the one who broke it is a company` MEANS
            CONSIDER `who broke it`
            WHEN `a company or other body corporate that broke it` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `ss 550, 558A, 558B -- who else I can bring the case against`

-- s 550(1): "A person who is involved in a contravention of a civil remedy provision is taken to have contravened that
-- provision." (2): "A person is involved in a contravention ... if, and only if, the person: (a) has aided, abetted,
-- counselled or procured the contravention; or (b) has induced the contravention, whether by threats or promises or
-- otherwise; or (c) has been in any way, by act or omission, directly or indirectly, knowingly concerned in or party to
-- the contravention; or (d) has conspired with others to effect the contravention."
@export Can I also bring the case against a manager, director, adviser or other person involved in the contravention (s 550)?
GIVEN `they aided, abetted, counselled or procured it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they aided, abetted, counselled or procured the contravention
      `they induced it by threats, promises or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they induced it, by threats, promises or otherwise
      `they were knowingly concerned in it or party to it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they were knowingly concerned in, or party to, it, by act or omission, directly or indirectly (for example, a manager who knew the pay rates were below the award and set them)
      `they conspired with others to bring it about` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they conspired with others to bring it about
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I also sue the person involved` IF
        `they aided, abetted, counselled or procured it`
    OR  `they induced it by threats, promises or otherwise`
    OR  `they were knowingly concerned in it or party to it`
    OR  `they conspired with others to bring it about`

-- s 558A: a franchisee entity is a franchisee whose business "is substantially or materially associated with
-- intellectual property relating to the franchise"; a responsible franchisor entity "has a significant degree of
-- influence or control over the franchisee entity's affairs".
-- s 558B(1): a responsible franchisor entity contravenes if the franchisee employer contravenes a provision in (7), in
-- its capacity as franchisee, and the franchisor or one of its officers "knew or could reasonably be expected to have
-- known that the contravention ... would occur", or that one "of the same or a similar character was likely to occur".
-- (2): the same for a body corporate whose subsidiary is the employer. (3): not if "the person had taken reasonable
-- steps to prevent a contravention ... of the same or a similar character". (7) lists ss 44, 45, 50, 280, 293, 305,
-- 323(1), 323(3), 325(1), 325(1A), 328, 357(1), 358, 359, 535 and others -- not the general protections, sexual
-- harassment or bullying provisions.
DECLARE `Who is above my employer` IS ONE OF
    `a franchisor of my employer's franchise`
    `a company of which my employer is a subsidiary`

@export Can I also bring the case against my employer's franchisor or holding company (ss 558A, 558B)?
GIVEN `who is above my employer` IS A `Who is above my employer` @desc Who you want to bring the case against: the franchisor of your employer's franchise; or a company of which your employer is a subsidiary
      `the contravention is one s 558B(7) lists` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the contravention is of the NES, an award, an agreement, the minimum wage, paying in full or in money (s 323), an unreasonable requirement to pay (s 325), sham contracting (ss 357-359) or employee records (s 535) -- the kinds s 558B(7) lists
      `my employer's business is substantially associated with the franchise's intellectual property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a franchise: whether your employer's business under the franchise is substantially or materially associated with the franchise's brand or other intellectual property
      `the franchisor has significant influence or control over my employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a franchise: whether the franchisor has a significant degree of influence or control over your employer's affairs
      `my employer broke it as a franchisee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a franchise: whether your employer broke it in its capacity as franchisee (running the franchised business)
      `they knew or should have known it would happen or was likely` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they (or one of their officers) knew or could reasonably be expected to have known the contravention would happen, or that one of the same or a similar kind was likely
      `they had taken reasonable steps to prevent it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, at the time, they had taken reasonable steps to prevent a contravention of that kind (training, audits, a complaints system)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I also sue the franchisor or holding company` IF
        `the contravention is one s 558B(7) lists`
    AND `the relationship is one s 558B reaches`
    AND `they knew or should have known it would happen or was likely`
    AND (NOT `they had taken reasonable steps to prevent it`)
    WHERE
        `the relationship is one s 558B reaches` MEANS
            CONSIDER `who is above my employer`
            WHEN `a franchisor of my employer's franchise` THEN
                    `my employer's business is substantially associated with the franchise's intellectual property`
                AND `the franchisor has significant influence or control over my employer`
                AND `my employer broke it as a franchisee`
            WHEN `a company of which my employer is a subsidiary` THEN TRUE

§§ `ss 547, 570 -- interest, and the risk of paying costs`

-- s 547(1), (2): in an order (other than a penalty) for an amount a person was required to pay under the Act or a fair
-- work instrument, "the court must, on application, include an amount of interest in the sum ordered, unless good cause
-- is shown to the contrary." Whether good cause is shown is the court's finding: an INPUT.
@export Must the court add interest to the amount it orders my employer to pay me (s 547)?
GIVEN `the order is for an amount I was owed under the Act, an award or an agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the order is for an amount your employer was required to pay you under the Fair Work Act, a modern award or an enterprise agreement (not a penalty)
      `I ask for interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you apply for interest
      `good cause is shown against interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court finds good cause shown against including interest
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the court add interest` IF
        `the order is for an amount I was owed under the Act, an award or an agreement`
    AND `I ask for interest`
    AND (NOT `good cause is shown against interest`)

-- s 570(1): a party to court proceedings under the Act "may be ordered ... to pay costs incurred by another party ...
-- only in accordance with subsection (2)" (or ss 569, 569A, which are about the Commonwealth and the States). (2): "only
-- if: (a) the court is satisfied that the party instituted the proceedings vexatiously or without reasonable cause; or
-- (b) the court is satisfied that the party's unreasonable act or omission caused the other party to incur the costs;
-- or (c) the court is satisfied of both of the following: (i) the party unreasonably refused to participate in a matter
-- before the FWC; (ii) the matter arose from the same facts as the proceedings."
@export Can I be ordered to pay the other side's legal costs in my Fair Work court case (s 570)?
GIVEN `the court finds I brought the case vexatiously or without reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court is satisfied you started the case vexatiously or without reasonable cause
      `the court finds my unreasonable act or omission caused their costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court is satisfied that something unreasonable you did, or failed to do, caused the other side to incur the costs
      `the court finds I unreasonably refused to take part at the FWC on the same facts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court is satisfied you unreasonably refused to take part in an FWC matter that arose from the same facts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be ordered to pay costs` IF
        `the court finds I brought the case vexatiously or without reasonable cause`
    OR  `the court finds my unreasonable act or omission caused their costs`
    OR  `the court finds I unreasonably refused to take part at the FWC on the same facts`
